// run's own display normalization (0 dB) rather than on any single measured
// point, because every point in that region carries the rig's local shape: a
// small +3 dB presence rise at 4.5 kHz easing back out by
// 7 kHz, then a natural fall to -9 dB at 20 kHz. Every segment joins
// with zero slope, so there are no corners.
//
// The stored top end is that shape without any structure of its own.
// topEndRipple() adds the small, shallow features a real 1/6-octave sweep
// keeps on top of it - a broad rise around 2.7 kHz, a dip at 5.8 kHz, a
// peak near 4.3 kHz and a few tenth-of-a-decibel wiggles up top, all within
// +/-0.55 dB of the shape and faded in over 2.05-2.7 kHz so the join with
// the measured blend region stays smooth. The tamed overall form is what
// stays; the rig's own comb structure above 2 kHz stays out.
//
